chip ym2414
clock 3579545
samples 40000
# The preset logic as ymfm models it. An alternate 0x40 write (bit 7) sets a
# flag at 0x100+n; while it is set, a 0xE0+n write is also stored as the
# preset (0x140+n) and clears the flag, and an alternate 0xC0+n write is
# stored as the preset 0x160+n. Writing a channel to 0x08 copies the
# channel's presets back into 0xE0 and the alternate 0xC0 registers. So: a
# voice is set up with presets, damped with a short release and no reverb,
# and restored by 0x08; a channel with no presets is zeroed by 0x08.
0 w 0 08 1 00 0 40 1 01 0 60 1 7f 0 80 1 1f 0 a0 1 00 0 c0 1 00 0 e0 1 0f 0 48 1 01 0 68 1 7f 0 88 1 1f 0 a8 1 00 0 c8 1 00 0 e8 1 0f 0 50 1 01 0 70 1 7f 0 90 1 1f 0 b0 1 00 0 d0 1 00 0 f0 1 0f 0 58 1 01 0 78 1 00 0 98 1 1f 0 b8 1 00 0 d8 1 00 0 f8 1 0f 0 58 1 90 0 d8 1 a3 0 f8 1 2a 0 20 1 87 0 28 1 4a 0 30 1 01 0 38 1 00  # preset: waveform 1 flag, shift 2/reverb 3, SL 2/RR 10
0 w 0 20 1 c7
4000 w 0 20 1 87
8000 w 0 f8 1 0f 0 d8 1 20  # damp: RR 15, no reverb
8000 w 0 20 1 c7
12000 w 0 20 1 87
16000 w 0 08 1 00  # restore through 0x08
16000 w 0 20 1 c7
20000 w 0 20 1 87
24000 w 0 08 1 01 0 41 1 01 0 61 1 7f 0 81 1 1f 0 a1 1 00 0 c1 1 00 0 e1 1 0f 0 49 1 01 0 69 1 7f 0 89 1 1f 0 a9 1 00 0 c9 1 00 0 e9 1 0f 0 51 1 01 0 71 1 7f 0 91 1 1f 0 b1 1 00 0 d1 1 00 0 f1 1 0f 0 59 1 01 0 79 1 00 0 99 1 1f 0 b9 1 00 0 d9 1 00 0 f9 1 13 0 21 1 87 0 29 1 4a 0 31 1 01 0 39 1 00 0 08 1 02 0 08 1 01  # channel 1 without presets: 0x08 zeroes its SL/RR
24000 w 0 21 1 c7
30000 w 0 21 1 87
34000 w 0 41 1 80 0 c9 1 25 0 f1 1 33  # the flag of 0x41 sends alternate 0xC9 writes nowhere special
